# text = And it came to pass that he built a tower near the temple; yea, a very high tower, even so high that he could stand upon the top thereof and overlook the land of Shilom, and also the land of Shemlon, which was possessed by the Lamanites; and he could even look over all the land round about.
# sent_id = 300
# llm_note: sent_id 300 — AICTP. Long sentence. "built a tower near the temple" = ccomp. "yea, a very high tower" = appos/elaboration on "tower"(10), attach as appos. "even so high that he could stand … and overlook" = result clause advcl on "tower"(20). "upon the top thereof" = obl of stand. "overlook" = conj of stand. "land of Shilom" and "land of Shemlon" = coord obj. "which was possessed by the Lamanites" = relcl on Shemlon's land. Final "he could even look over all the land round about" = conj.
